Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dsi: acknowledge error summary after clearing sources

The later Qualcomm downstream handler leaves the error summary pending
until its peripheral causes are cleared and ignores processing when its
source mask is disabled. Follow that ordering instead of acknowledging the
summary before the detailed FIFO/timeout/PHY status. Keep existing
error masks, reset policy and display timings. This is a diagnostic
candidate for the measured recurring DSI IRQs; it does not claim to fix
HS underflow.

Link: https://android.googlesource.com/kernel/msm/+/ddc71b24ab0b8cb5bc73f6e9a89bdb48da052cd8/drivers/video/fbdev/msm/mdss_dsi_host.c
The older pinned Samsung tree still acknowledges the summary first.
---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/dsi_host.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/dsi_host.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/dsi_host.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/dsi_host.c
@@ -1742,6 +1742,9 @@
 	dsi_status(msm_host);
 	dsi_dln0_phy_err(msm_host);
 
+	/* W1C the summary after acknowledging all detailed error sources. */
+	dsi_intr_ctrl(msm_host, DSI_IRQ_ERROR, 1);
+
 	queue_work(msm_host->workqueue, &msm_host->err_work);
 }
 
@@ -1756,12 +1759,13 @@
 
 	spin_lock_irqsave(&msm_host->intr_lock, flags);
 	isr = dsi_read(msm_host, REG_DSI_INTR_CTRL);
-	dsi_write(msm_host, REG_DSI_INTR_CTRL, isr);
+	/* Clear the summary only after its peripheral causes are cleared. */
+	dsi_write(msm_host, REG_DSI_INTR_CTRL, isr & ~DSI_IRQ_ERROR);
 	spin_unlock_irqrestore(&msm_host->intr_lock, flags);
 
 	DBG("isr=0x%x, id=%d", isr, msm_host->id);
 
-	if (isr & DSI_IRQ_ERROR)
+	if ((isr & DSI_IRQ_ERROR) && (isr & DSI_IRQ_MASK_ERROR))
 		dsi_error(msm_host, isr);
 
 	if (isr & DSI_IRQ_VIDEO_DONE)
